  {
    "title": "File:Tidal wave warning sign near Breskens.jpg",
    "url": "https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Tidal_wave_warning_sign_near_Breskens.jpg/1280px-Tidal_wave_warning_sign_near_Breskens.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail",
    "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tidal_wave_warning_sign_near_Breskens.jpg",
    "original_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4e/Tidal_wave_warning_sign_near_Breskens.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
    "license": "CC BY 4.0",
    "artist": "<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Mitsjol&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Mitsjol (page does not exist)\">Mitsjol</a>",
    "description": "A warning sign located near Breskens, positioned along a coastal area prone to tidal waves caused by passing sea-going vessels. The sign features a warning symbol and a figure being knocked over by a wave. The text on the sign is written in three languages—Dutch, English, and German. The text informs readers that passing ships can sometimes create hazardous tidal waves, urging caution, especially when the water appears to be drawing back. Behind the sign, the coastal landscape and water are visible."
  },
